# What does NOT go to Vercel.
#
# The deployment upload is capped at 10mb and this repository is far larger than the
# application inside it: `services/` alone is a Rust workspace with build artifacts, and
# `evidence-dumps/` is the captured reference the gates verify against. Neither is read
# by `vite build`, which was confirmed before writing this — nothing under `src/`,
# `vite.config.ts` or `svelte.config.js` resolves a path outside `src/` and `static/`.
#
# Keep `scripts/` and the config files: they are small, and `prepare` runs during install.

# The Rust workspace. Deployed separately to its own host; the SFU needs UDP and a
# static public address, which Vercel does not offer.
services/

# Captured reference evidence and the documentation built from it. Test-time inputs.
evidence-dumps/
docs/
ops/
css-modals/

# Local and CI artifacts.
.data/
build/
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
e2e/

# Editor and agent tooling installed into the tree by other tools.
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json

# Notes, never runtime inputs.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
